  "historical": {
    "title": "Why the metformin charge was higher in September",
    "body": "Completed charges are established by two paid pharmacy claims for metformin 500 mg tablets, quantity 60 for a 30-day supply. On August 18, 2026, the claim at Oak Street Pharmacy was processed under the preferred retail cost-share category and the member paid $8.00. On September 16, 2026, the claim at Lakeview Pharmacy was processed under the standard retail cost-share category and the member paid $27.00.\n\nThe pharmacy classifications support that Oak Street Pharmacy was preferred retail on August 18 and Lakeview Pharmacy was standard retail on September 16. The selected policy states that, for the recorded conditions, a matched 30-day metformin 500 mg supply is $8 at preferred retail and $27 at standard retail. The higher September charge is therefore supported by the different applied pharmacy cost-share category.",
    "sourceLabel": "System record · claims · simulated; Governed guidance · scripting · simulated",
    "causeSupported": true,
    "chargesEstablished": true
  },
